Aim

To deploy a basic web application using Oracle Cloud compute services with networking and security configurations.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Internet Connection
Compute Instance
SSH Client (Windows PowerShell or PuTTY)
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console

Login using:

Username
Password
Step 2: Create Compute Instance

Go to:

☰ Menu
→ Compute
→ Instances

Click:

Create Instance

Step 3: Configure Instance

Fill details:

Field	Value
Name	WebServer
Image	Oracle Linux
Shape	VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro

Keep default options.

Step 4: Generate SSH Keys

Under:

Add SSH Keys

Select:

Generate a key pair for me

Click:

Save Private Key
and
Save Public Key

Important:

Keep private key safely.
Step 5: Create Instance

Click:

Create

Wait 2–5 minutes.

Instance status becomes:

Running

Step 6: Copy Public IP Address

Inside instance page:

Copy:

Public IP Address

Example:

129.xxx.xxx.xxx
Step 7: Open Security Rules

Go to:

Networking
→ Virtual Cloud Networks

Open your VCN.

Click:

Security Lists

Open:

Default Security List

Step 8: Add Ingress Rule for HTTP

Click:

Add Ingress Rules

Enter:

Field	Value
Source CIDR	0.0.0.0/0
Destination Port Range	80

Click:

Add Ingress Rules

This allows website access.

Step 9: Connect to Instance Using SSH

Open PowerShell in Windows.

Run:

ssh -i privatekey.key opc@your_public_ip

Example:

ssh -i ssh-key-2026.key opc@129.xxx.xxx.xxx

Type:

yes

You are connected successfully.

Step 10: Install Apache Web Server

Run commands one by one:

sudo yum update -y

Then:

sudo yum install httpd -y
Step 11: Start Apache Server

Run:

sudo systemctl start httpd

Enable auto start:

sudo systemctl enable httpd
Step 12: Create Web Page

Run:

sudo nano /var/www/html/index.html

Add:

<html>
<head>
<title>My Web App</title>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Hello from Oracle Cloud</h1>
</body>
</html>

Save:

CTRL + O
Enter
CTRL + X
Step 13: Open Website in Browser

Open browser.

Type:

http://your_public_ip

Example:

http://129.xxx.xxx.xxx
Step 14: Verify Output

Browser displays:

Hello from Oracle Cloud

This confirms deployment success.

Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Created compute instance
Configured networking
Installed Apache web server
Created web page
Accessed application using public IP

Basic web application deployed successfully in Oracle Cloud.
